<title>UK: NEF Japan sets 150 million mark seven-year bond.</title>
<headline>NEF Japan sets 150 million mark seven-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi and Bayerische Landesbank.</p>
<p> BORROWER   NORTH EAST FINANCE OF JAPAN</p>
<p>GUARANTOR  JAPAN</p>
<p> AMT    150 MLN DEM   COUPON     5.875     MATURITY    15.OCT.03</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.753   PAY DATE    15.OCT.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.50	REOFFER    99.553    SPREAD	+14 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	=	   LISTING    FFT/MUN   PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMS US/UK/DE/JP</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    GERMAN    HOME CTRY  JAPAN     TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.30	SELL CONC  1.95	LISTING FEE 0.25</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND SEPTEMBER 2003 BUND</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
